{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will fill him.</b> Like <i>and Joshua son of Nun was filled with the spirit of wisdom</i> (Deuteronomy 34:9). And it is written <i>and the spirit of HaShem shall rest upon him</i> (Isaiah 11:2), and it explains what the spirit of HaShem is: <i>and it is the spirit of wisdom and understanding</i> (ibid.). Wisdom is the forms engraved in the hindmost part of the brain, and the word תבונה, likewise בינה, is from the root בין, and it is the form that stands between the form of knowledge and the form of wisdom, corresponding to the middle ventricle of the brain — for wisdom corresponds to the hindmost ventricle, and knowledge, joined by the ventricles of the brain over the forehead, [comes] from sense-perceptions. In the language of Ishmael they call knowledge אלתכיי״ל, and understanding אלפכר״ה, and wisdom אלחכמ״ה. Now Bezalel was filled with all wisdom: in reckoning and measures and proportions and the craft of the heavens and the wisdom of generation and the secret of the soul. And he had superiority over all the men of his generation, for he knew every craft, since many wise-hearted men did not know even a single craft. Therefore it is written <i>and in every craft</i>, with a vav."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Resolved Deuteronomy citation from abbreviation דברי׳. The transliterated Arabic terms left in Ibn Ezra's Hebrew orthography; they correspond to Arabic al-ʿaql, al-fikra, and al-ḥikma."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:36.330224327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}